  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Support the presser – five v four",
  "description": "Half a rink with a goalkeeper in goal. Four blue attackers plus a free player, J, against five red defenders. J always starts with the ball at the centre line and only plays as support from behind.\n\nRed have an extra player and must use it: one goes at the ball, one supports close by and the rest cover the space in front of goal. The attempt ends when red win the ball, after a goal or when the ball goes over the end line or the boards. Swap attack and defence after ten attempts and change the free player at the same time.\n\nBuild on it: put two small goals on the centre line for red to score in after winning the ball. Harder: five v five, with J free to play anywhere. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The supporting defender stands a few metres at an angle behind the presser – close enough to take over at once."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "When the ball moves on, the supporter becomes the new presser and the old presser drops back to support."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "The rest move with the ball and stay compact – no free space straight in front of goal."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "The goalkeeper sees the whole picture: organise the defence with your voice."
    }
  ],
